sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch04-24> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The dominance of partial differential equations as models in science is in many respects a historical accident of their being solvable by explicit formulas before computers; had computers come earlier, scientific modeling would probably be very different.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Partial differential equations predominate largely by historical accident";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 4, “Systems Based on Numbers”; section “Partial Differential Equations” (from p. 161), p. 162. Scope: history of mathematical modeling in physics and other sciences"
}
